  "worked_solution": "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3+4y-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4y+3 & =0 \\\\ (y-1)(y-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $y=1,\\,3.$ So, we need to integrate from $y=1$ to $y=3.$ \n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}yf(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{3}y(-3+4y-{y}^{2})\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
